smartinit.v3.5.1  Q3FY16 

January 2016 NAM/DGEX smartinit upgrade to coincide with RTMA/URMA upgrade (see docs/README for more details on changes)

- Converted to phase 2.
- Added new grid specifications for expanded CONUS Nest (grid 188) and Puerto Rico 1.25 km domain (grid 254). Changed Puerto Rico 
  domain back to 2.5 km domain (for this implementation only).
- Added local versions of the source codes and executables of cnvgrib, wgrib2, overgridnum_grib and nam_prdgen.
- Added two new fields: ceiling height and Mesinger mean sea-level pressure. 
- Added hourly total cloud cover, land/sea mask for CONUS Nest, and fixed wind gust, DX/DY and bitmap bugs.
- Added hours 00, 10, 11, and 12 to *ak_rtmages* smartinit output files.
- Converted all hourly files and *ak_rtmages* files to GRIB2 for RTMA/URMA.
- Added GRIB2 option for future implementation using Eric's NAM parallel (this option is not used yet; will be implemented in
  Q4FY16).
- Added option that determines how frequently to write out AWIPS files (hourly, 3-hourly, etc...). 
- Added hourly WMO header files and two new fields (ceiling height and MSLP) to the WMO header files.
- Changed grid 188 back to grib 184 (using copygb).  CONUS Nest output files are grid 184.  This was done so the AWIPS 
  header parm files would not have to be recreated for grid 188. Twelve GRIB1 grid 188 files are added to the output directory, 
  for use in RTMA/URMA and they are called:

  nam.t${cyc}z.smartconus2p5${hh}.tm00_wexp

- Added changes to meet NCO's phase 2 standards.
- Added ceiling height, Mesinger MSLP to GDAS option

===================================================================================
1.  Converted to phase 2  

    * The v3.5.1 system was converted to phase 2; specifically the script parm/smart_para_config was changed.

2.  Added new grid specifications for expanded CONUS Nest (grid 188) and Puerto Rico 1.25 km domain (grid 254). Puerto Rico 1.25
    km domain is not being used in this implementation.

    * Added Terrain, Land/Sea Mask, weight and master parm files for new expanded CONUS Nest domain (grid 188) and Puerto Rico 1.25        km domain (grid 254). Expanded CONUS Nest is using consensus Terrain and Land/Sea Mask.
    * For this implementation, Puerto Rico 1.25 km domain was set back to the 2.5 km domain.

3.  Added local versions of the source codes and executables of cnvgrib, wgrib2, nam_prdgen and overgridnum_grib.

        sorc/smartinit_cnvgrib.fd
        sorc/smartinit_prdgen.fd
        sorc/smartinit_wgrib2.cd
        sorc/smartinit_overgridnum_grib.fd

    * Added local versions of cnvgrib, wgrib2, nam_prdgen to jobs/JNAM_SMINIT and jobs/JDGEX_SMINIT

4.  Added new fields: ceiling height and MSLP.  

    * Added ceiling height to the master parm files. 
    * Uses ceiling height and MSLP from OPS *bgdawp* files.

5.  Added land/sea mask for CONUS Nest and hourly total cloud cover.  Fixed bugs found involving wind gusts, 
    Haines Index and Ceiling Height bitmap and DX/DY for *ak_rtmages* and DGEX AK domains.

    * Added hourly total cloud cover
    * CONUS Nest uses land/sea mask instead of vegetation type to define temps/dewpoint/winds near coastlines 
    * Changed grid spacing in code for Puerto Rico from 2500 km to 1250 km (changed back to 2500 km for this implementation).
    * Wind gust is now being read in and used for evaluating wind gust for intermediate hours
    * Changed DX/DY to 6000 km for *ak_rtmages* and DGEX AK files.
    * Set Haines Index and Ceiling Height to SPVAL for bitmap

6.  Added hours 00 and 10, 11, and 12 to *ak_rtmages* files.

7.  Converted all hourly files and *ak_rtmages* files to GRIB2 for RTMA/URMA.

8.  Added GRIB switch to ush/smartinit.sh.  
    
    export grib=1 ; for using OPS NAM GRIB1 data
    export grib=2 ; for using parallel NAM GRIB2 data

9.  Added GRIB2 option for future implementation using Eric's NAM parallel (this option is not used yet; will be implemented in
    Q3FY16).

  * added GRIB2 master parm files
  * replaced nam_prdgen with wgrib2
  * added parallel wgrib2
  * added GRIB2 specs for each grid
  * uses parallel 3 km NAM Nests
  * wgrib2 uses nearest neighbor interpolation for 2.5 km CONUS Nest, 3 km Hawaiinest, and 3 km Alaskanest; uses budget for 
    precipitation/snow fields; and bilinear interpolation for all other grids.

10. Added option that determines how frequently to write out AWIPS files (hourly, 3-hourly, etc...). Option is set to hourly
    for this implementation.

    * Added hourly WMO header files and two new fields (ceiling height and MSLP) to the WMO header files.

    Note: There are no new datacards delivered with this package. They will be updated  prior to the start of the
          30-day parallel if they are available. If they are not, we will use the old data files 
          and update them in our next implementation.

11. Changed grid 188 back to grid 184(using copygb).  CONUS Nest output files are now grid 184.  This was done so the AWIPS 
    header parm files would not have to be recreated for grid 188.  Twelve GRIB1 grid 188 files are added to output directory,
    for use in RTMA/URMA:

    nam.t${cyc}z.smartconus2p5${hh}.tm00_wexp

12. Added changes to meet NCO's phase 2 standards: 

    * removed all unused J-jobs /jobs directory
    * removed files in exec/ directory
    * modified jobs/JNAM_SMINIT and jobs/JDGEX_SMINIT
    * modified ush/smartinit.sh, ush/dgex_smartinit.sh, and ush/dng_awp.sh
    * updated docs/README, docs/smartinit.ver
    * modified parm/smart_para_config

13. Added ceiling height, and Mesinger MSLP to GDAS option

#===============================================================================
 IMPLEMENTATION INSTRUCTIONS 
#===============================================================================
1.  svn checkout https://svnemc.ncep.noaa.gov/projects/smartinit/tags/RB-v3.5.1 smartinit.v3.5.1

    to set up and run on WCOSS phase 2.

2.  Build sorc codes smartinit.fd, smartprecip.fd, smartinit_cnvgrib.fd, smartinit_prdgen.fd, smartinit_wgrib2.cd
       
	The modulefile used for the build is in modulefiles/SMARTINIT/v3.5.1.  Copy it to a location from which it can
	be loaded (/nwprod2/modulefiles/SMARTINIT or something similar). 

	In the smartinit main directory "smartinit.v3.5.1" type
		./build_smartinit.scr
	to compile the codes sequentially.  All executables will be copied over to the smartinit "exec" directory.

3.  Will be running ak_rtmages for 00-12 hours now.  Therefore, create ecf/sminit_ak/akrtmages/jnam_sminit_akrtmages_f00.ecf and             ecf/sminit_ak/akrtmages/jnam_sminit_akrtmages_f12.ecf.  Change 5 instances of HH (e.g. 06) to 00 and 12 for each script,             respectively. 

4.  Use ...docs/smartinit.ver file if desired to set
      model_ver=v3.5.1  parameter

